{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/admissions-counselor-assistant-director": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director",
      "description": "Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. University Benefits Holy Family University takes pride in offering a range of meaningful and flexible benefits designed to promote the health and wellness of our employees and their dependents. Our comprehensive benefits and resources focus on physical, mental and financial wellness to include medical, prescription, dental and vision. We did not stop there; we also offer our employees the following fringe benefits and more. Commuter Benefits: Transit and park benefits through pre-tax payroll deductions Half-Day Fridays: Enjoy half day Fridays in the summer 403(b) Retirement: Discretionary match up to 5%; vested immediately Time Off: 12 Paid Holidays, Vacation, Personal, Sick Days and a week off for Winter Break Tuition Benefits: Employees or dependents pursuing a first Undergraduate Degree receive 100% tuition remission; employees pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 100% tuition remission; eligible dependents pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 50% tuition discount. Alpha House: 50% Discount for Nursery, Pre-K and Kindergarten Position Summary We are seeking an Admissions Counselor or Assistant Director (dependent upon experience), responsible for the recruitment of undergraduate students to the institution.  Duties include representing the university at various off-campus events, application/prospect management, meeting with students and families, and coordinating special recruitment programs and events. Employees must understand the mission of Catholic Higher education and be committed to the core values, mission, goals, and objectives of Holy Family University. Candidates should be open to working a flexible schedule that will include evening and weekend work during certain times of the year. A valid driver’s license in good standing and ability to travel via automobile for extensive local and regional travel is required. Responsibilities (not all inclusive): Articulate the university's admissions process, programs and mission to prospective students. Manage assigned travel territory and meet assigned enrollment goals. Evaluate and manage all applicants assigned by territory/major.  Timely review and assessment for all applications assigned is required. Assist with the planning and execution of recruitment events. Establish and maintain good rapport and relationship with counselors and teachers in the assigned schools. Qualifications A bachelor’s degree required and 1-2 years of college admissions education experience preferred.  Other higher education-related experience will be considered. Experience with supervising student-workers or other employees is a plus. Ability to exercise sound professional judgment in interacting with students, faculty, staff and internal/external stakeholders is required. Strong communication skills. Experience with Microsoft Office suite of applications required. CRM software experience preferred. Candidates should be open to working a flexible schedule that will include evening and weekend work during certain times of the year. A valid driver’s license in good standing and ability to travel via automobile is required. Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter and resume. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/assistant-athletic-trainer": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Assistant Athletic Trainer | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Assistant Athletic Trainer About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Assistant Athletic Trainer More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. University Benefits Holy Family University takes pride in offering a range of meaningful and flexible benefits designed to promote the health and wellness of our employees and their dependents. Our comprehensive benefits and resources focus on physical, mental and financial wellness to include medical, prescription, dental and vision. We did not stop there; we also offer our employees the following fringe benefits and more. Commuter Benefits: Transit and park benefits through pre-tax payroll deductions Half-Day Fridays: Enjoy half day Fridays in the summer 403(b) Retirement: Discretionary match up to 5%; vested immediately Time Off: 12 Paid Holidays, Vacation, Personal, Sick Days and a week off for Winter Break Tuition Benefits: Employees or dependents pursuing a first Undergraduate Degree receive 100% tuition remission; employees pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 100% tuition remission; eligible dependents pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 50% tuition discount. Alpha House: 50% Discount for Nursery, Pre-K and Kindergarten Position Summary To be responsible for administering quality healthcare through practice and game coverage, injury prevention, evaluation, management, treatment of new and pre-existing injuries, short & long-term rehabilitation of athletic injuries, education and counseling of student-athletes, athletics- related health care administration and ensure compliance with NCAA legislation, the Board of Certification for the Athletic Trainer, and Pennsylvania State Board of Medicine. The Certified Athletic Trainer is the primary person to make decisions on the playing status of all athletes. The Certified Athletic Trainer is accountable for the daily maintenance of the athletic training room and related equipment and supplies. The employee must understand and embrace the mission of Catholic higher education and must commit to the mission, goals and objectives of Holy Family University in word and deed. Direct Reports N/A Essential Functions Job duties that must be performed, with or without reasonable accommodation, and may include any of the following tasks, knowledge, skills and other characteristics. This job description is illustrative and is not a comprehensive listing of all functions and tasks performed by incumbents in this position. Provide athletic training coverage at all assigned games, events, and practices. This includes providing first aid care and acting in a first responder capacity as necessary. Primary sport assignments for this role would include men’s lacrosse and men’s basketball. Ability to travel with men’s lacrosse is required. Assist the Head Athletic Trainer with planning, organizing, and directing the use of the athletic training clinics for care and treatment of student-athletes. This includes the enforcement of all applicable athletic training related policies and procedures. Provide appropriate HIPAA compliant communication regarding medical conditions to the Head Athletic Trainer and members of the athletic department staff. Verifying all necessary aspects of pre-participation paperwork and maintaining complete and accurate records of all services provided and all athletic injuries on applicable injury tracking software. Assist student-athletes to safely return to activity after injuries. This includes evaluating acute and chronic athletic related injuries, creating individualized treatment and rehabilitation protocols for the management of acute and chronic sports-related injuries. Work collaboratively with the sports performance staff and coaching staff to ensure all safe and health environment for the student athletes. Coordinate care with the team physician and make referrals to other members of the healthcare team as necessary. Review secondary insurance information and claims. Remain current with research in sports medicine and related fields and commit to use of evidence-based practice in order to provide a high level of care to support the student athlete experience. Maintain daily upkeep of the athletic training room to comply with healthcare setting standards, including HIPAA and OSHA standards. Maintain accurate inventory of supplies and place orders as needed with approval of the Head Athletic Trainer. Site supervision as assigned Non-Essential Duties/Responsibilities Any other duties as assigned. General Expectations Employees are expected to accomplish assigned duties in an efficient, effective and competent manner and to strive for improvement and excellence in all work performed.  Employees must understand the mission and demonstrate the core values of the University. Additionally, demonstrate the ability to work with diverse personalities, and harmoniously with students, faculty and staff, and the public.  Employees are expected to follow and abide by all University policies, rules, regulations and guidelines. Education & Experience Requirements Bachelor’s degree in athletic training required. Master’s degree preferred. Athletic training experience in the collegiate setting preferred. Previous experience with men’s or boy’s lacrosse is preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to perform comprehensive injury evaluations, develop treatment and rehabilitation protocols using evidence-based medicine, advanced knowledge of anatomy and physiology, generation of inventory reports, proficiency in injury tracking software and documentation of injuries. Knowledge of and ability to follow university policies and procedures. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with the campus community. Knowledge of rules and regulations from applicable governing bodies, such as the NCAA, the Board of Certification, the Pennsylvania State Board of Medicine/State Board of Osteopathic Medicine, as well as applicable laws/acts such as Title IX, HIPAA, and FERPA. Game day management and best practices Must have sound independent judgment and ability to maintain discretion and confidentiality. Ability to work independently. Ability to work and communicate effectively with a diverse population. Excellent attention to detail, problem solving, analytical, communication (verbal and written), interpersonal, and customer service skills. Understanding of organizational processes and strong follow-up skills. Must demonstrate good time management and project management skills. Ability to travel with the men’s lacrosse team is required. Work Environment Operates in an office environment, that may have frequent interruptions.  The area is well-lit, temperature controlled and free from hazards. Noise level is can vary from quiet to loud throughout the course of a work day. The ability to work in an outdoor environment, including in elements such as wind, rain, and snow, in temperatures varying from 15°F to 100°+ F, is required. Physical Requirements Communicates frequently, in person, over the phone, or via a computer.  Hearing is needed for extensive telephone and in person communication. Regularly required to sit or stand for long periods of time; use hands to finger, handle or feel; reach with hands and arms. Manual dexterity is needed in order to operate a computer keyboard and provide multiple sessions of manual therapy throughout the course of a day. Operates standard office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, filing cabinets and fax machines. The ability to move safely yet swiftly (e.g., running/jogging, walking/jogging up and down stairs or hills) when necessary is required. The ability to lift 50+ pounds and physically assist injured parties in standing, sitting, or walking is required. The ability to handle physically strenuous tasks, such as providing emergency injury management (CPR, neck/spine stabilization) for prolonged periods of time. Certification/Licensure Current National Board of Certification Athletic Training Certification required Current Pennsylvania Board of Medicine License in Athletic Training required Current First Aid/CPR/AED for the Professional Rescuer Certification Other important information Should teleworking become necessary, employee must be willing and able to perform all parts of this job description while working from home, on campus or a combination, and be proficient or willing to become proficient in the technology needed to work remotely. Night and weekend availability is required. Ability to drive a 15-passenger van is required Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter and resume. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/assistant-professor-counseling-psychology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. University Benefits Holy Family University takes pride in offering a range of meaningful and flexible benefits designed to promote the health and wellness of our employees and their dependents. Our comprehensive benefits and resources focus on physical, mental and financial wellness to include medical, prescription, dental and vision. We did not stop there; we also offer our employees the following fringe benefits and more. Commuter Benefits: Transit and park benefits through pre-tax payroll deductions 403(b) Retirement: Discretionary match up to 5%; vested immediately Time Off: Paid Holidays, Sick Days and a week off for Winter Break Tuition Benefits: Employees or dependents pursuing a first Undergraduate Degree receive 100% tuition remission; employees pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 100% tuition remission; eligible dependents pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 50% tuition discount Alpha House: 50% Discount for Nursery, Pre-K and Kindergarten Position Summary The School of Arts and Sciences invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology, with a start date of August 2027. All employees must understand the mission of Catholic higher education and be committed to the core values, mission, goals, and objectives of Holy Family University. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in graduate teaching and be enthusiastic about engaging students in interdisciplinary approaches to contemporary issues. The successful candidate should have demonstrated excellence in teaching higher education. Although the area of specialization is open, the department seeks a candidate who will be able to teach classes in the Master’s in Counseling Psychology program which delivers courses in-person in the evenings, online synchronous, and in fully online asynchronous. It is expected that the successful candidate will maintain a commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Duties and Responsibilities (not all-inclusive) Teaching courses within the Masters of Counseling Psychology Program. There is strong interest in candidates who are able to teach courses in cognitive and affective processes, psychopharmacology, and physiological bases of behavior Maintaining academic excellence in the classroom Advising and mentoring students in the Masters of Counseling Psychology program Sustaining an active research and scholarship agenda Participation in school- and university-wide committees, initiatives, and other service opportunities Education & Experience Requirements Candidates must hold a Psy.D. or Ph.D. degree in psychology (or a closely related field) Licensed Clinical Psychologist Previous teaching experience 1-3 years Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, a statement of research interests, a list of courses taught, and complete graduate transcripts. Three letters of recommendation must be sent from the senders to the hiring manager at careers@holyfamly.edu . Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/financial-services-specialist": {
      "title": "Financial Services Specialist",
      "description": "Financial Services Specialist | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Financial Services Specialist About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Financial Services Specialist More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. University Benefits Holy Family University takes pride in offering a range of meaningful and flexible benefits designed to promote the health and wellness of our employees and their dependents. Our comprehensive benefits and resources focus on physical, mental and financial wellness to include medical, prescription, dental and vision. We did not stop there; we also offer our employees the following fringe benefits and more. Commuter Benefits: Transit and park benefits through pre-tax payroll deductions Half-Day Fridays: Enjoy half day Fridays in the summer 403(b) Retirement: Discretionary match up to 5%; vested immediately Time Off: 12 Paid Holidays, Vacation, Personal, Sick Days and a week off for Winter Break Tuition Benefits: Employees or dependents pursuing a first Undergraduate Degree receive 100% tuition remission; employees pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 100% tuition remission; eligible dependents pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 50% tuition discount. Alpha House: 50% Discount for Nursery, Pre-K and Kindergarten Position Summary The Financial Services Specialist plays a critical role in supporting the financial operations of the Student Accounts office at Holy Family University. This position is responsible for providing customer service related to student account transactions. The Financial Services Specialist works closely with students, parents, staff, and various campus departments to ensure accurate and timely billing, collection of tuition and fees, along with the day-to-day operations of the Student Accounts office.  The Financial Services Specialist is expected to learn both Student Accounts and Financial Aid operations to better serve our students. General Expectations of Holy Family University employees: Uphold the mission and core values of Holy Family University, supporting the education of students to assume lifelong responsibilities towards God, society and self. Accomplish assigned duties in an efficient, effective and competent manner. Strive for improvement and excellence in all work performed. Demonstrate the ability to effectively interact with and work with students, faculty, staff and the public. Follow and abide by all University policies, rules, regulations and guidelines. If an alternative work location is permitted or should become necessary, the employee must be able to perform all parts of this job description while working away from the office, on campus or a combination, and be proficient or willing to become proficient in the technology needed to work away from the office. Essential Functions Job duties must be performed, with or without reasonable accommodation, and may include any of the following tasks, knowledge, skills and other characteristics.  This position description is illustrative and is not a comprehensive listing of all functions and tasks performed by incumbents in this position. Billing and Payment Processing Assist in the communication of student billing statements, ensuring accuracy and completeness. Record all payments as they are received, including cash, checks, credit card payments, and wire transfers, by the end of the business day. Ensure that financial aid, scholarships, and third-party payments are accurately applied to student accounts. Monitor and reconcile student accounts to ensure accurate balances and charges. Audit and clear balances daily so that a hold is removed within 1 business day of account activity.  During peak times (resident move-in weeks, academic registration periods), reconciliations should happen hourly. Update housing clearance documents with every change in status. Set up and monitor payment plans. Assist in adding Tiger Tag funds, adding/dropping housing related charges, and adding/dropping commuter meal plans. Review and apply withdrawal procedures, returning funds, and student refunds. Reconcile cash receipts to cash collected at the end of the business day. Customer Service and Support Serve as a point of contact for students, parents, and staff regarding inquiries related to tuition, fees, billing, and payments. Resolve billing issues and answer questions concerning tuition charges, financial holds, and account balances. Assist students in understanding payment plans and help them navigate available payment options. Answer detailed financial aid inquiries without needing to redirect students to that office. Respond to all emails and voicemails (both individual and office account) within one business day. Data Management and Reporting Maintain accurate records of student financial transactions and ensure compliance with institutional policies and procedures. Generate financial reports on student accounts and billing. Assist in audits of student accounts and help ensure proper documentation is maintained. Document every interaction with students in Colleague. Additional Responsibilities Provide backup support for Accounts Receivable, Financial Aid, and other office personnel during peak times or when necessary. Stay informed of industry trends, regulations, and best practices related to higher education finance and billing. Non-Essential Duties/Responsibilities Any other duties as assigned. Education & Experience Requirements High School Diploma required; Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Business Administration, Finance, or a related field is preferred. (Equivalent work experience may be considered in lieu of a degree.) Minimum of 3 years of experience in a financial or administrative role, preferably in a higher education setting. Experience with financial software systems (preferably Colleague) and Microsoft Office Suite. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Strong knowledge of student account management, billing processes, and financial regulations within higher education. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with attention to detail. Excellent customer service and communication skills, both written and verbal. Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize effectively in a fast-paced environment. Knowledge of higher education financial aid programs and policies. Ability to work collaboratively with a diverse group of students, parents, and staff. Familiarity with FERPA (Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act) and other relevant student privacy and financial regulations. Work Environment Operates in an office environment that may have frequent interruptions. The area is well-lit, temperature controlled and free from hazards. Noise level is generally quiet to moderate. Physical Requirements Communicates frequently, in person, over the phone, or via a computer. Hearing is needed for extensive telephone and in person communication. Regularly required to sit for long periods of time; use hands to finger, handle or feel; reach with hands and arms. Manual dexterity is needed in order to operate a computer keyboard. Operates standard office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, filing cabinets and fax machines. Other important information Evening or weekend work will be required during peak billing periods or for special projects. Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter and resume. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/head-womens-soccer-coach": {
      "title": "Head Women’s Soccer Coach",
      "description": "Head Women’s Soccer Coach | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Head Women’s Soccer Coach About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Head Women’s Soccer Coach More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. Position Summary The Head Coach is responsible for coaching, directing and executing all aspects of an NCAA Division II program, and operating the program with integrity and in a welcoming manner that complies with NCAA, Central Atlantic Collegiate Conference, Athletics Department and University rules and regulations.  The Head Coach will cooperate and work harmoniously within the athletics department, and the campus community, as appropriate, in carrying out the philosophy and objectives of the intercollegiate athletic program. Additionally, will assist as site supervisor for various sporting events, and participate in Student Affairs programming, as scheduled. The employee must understand and embrace the mission of Catholic higher education and must commit to the mission, goals and objectives of Holy Family University in word and deed. Direct Reports Coaching Staff Essential Functions Job duties that must be performed, with or without reasonable accommodation, and may include any of the following tasks, knowledge, skills and other characteristics. This job description is illustrative and is not a comprehensive listing of all functions and tasks performed by incumbents in this position. Responsible for administering all aspects of the sport program including but not limited to: quality coaching and instruction; compliance; recruiting; promoting/fundraising; team travel arrangements; maintaining equipment; community service initiatives; supervising assistants; monitoring academic progress of student-athletes; and fulfilling other such duties as they arise or as assigned. Required to be thoroughly familiar with and comply with all University, Department, NCAA, and CACC policies, rules and regulations, and disseminate such information to assistant coaches and student-athletes, as appropriate. Collaborate with and provide all necessary information to the Assistant Director of Athletics for Compliance and ensure all NCAA and CACC rules and regulations are adhered to. This includes annual and on time completion of the NCAA Recruiting certification test. Model good sportsmanship behavior and maintain appropriate conduct towards student-athletes, fans, parents, officials, spectators and community. Serve as ambassador at University events and Open Houses. Foster a healthy environment for student-athletes while promoting sportsmanship and ethical behavior. Responsible for assisting in the preparation of, and adhering to, deadlines and specific dates for the timely completion of all forms and related materials. Effectively manage and strictly adhere to travel, recruiting, scholarship and departmental budgets. Obtain approval from the Athletic Director, in advance of any variance. Collaborate with Strength & Conditioning Coach/Athletic Training Staff to ensure the physical health, safety and well-being of student-athletes. Provide on-site supervision during all team activities. Moderate the Student-Athlete Advisory Committee (SAAC) including scheduling meetings, planning special events, performing community service and attending Conference SAAC meetings. Assist with site supervision and preparation of athletic programs, special events and home contests, for other sports, as scheduled. Assist, plan, moderate and supervise outside vendors and events in collaboration with the Assistant Director of Athletics for Daily Operations. Coordinate, track and distribute apparel/equipment orders for the Department of Athletics. Responsible for developing and executing fundraising initiatives and events. General Expectations Employees are expected to accomplish assigned duties in an efficient, effective and competent manner and to strive for improvement and excellence in all work performed.  Employees must understand the mission and demonstrate the core values of the University. Additionally, demonstrate the ability to work with diverse personalities, and harmoniously with students, faculty and staff, and the public.  Employees are expected to follow and abide by all University policies, rules, regulations and guidelines. Complete all necessary Compliance and Institutional documentation as required. Education & Experience Requirements Bachelor’s degree preferred At least two years’ collegiate level coaching and recruiting experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of and ability to follow university policies and procedures. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with the campus community. Knowledge of and ability to follow university policies and procedures. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with the campus community. Proficient with computer software (e.g. Word, Excel, PowerPoint etc.) NCAA sport rules and regulations Game day management and best practices Must have sound independent judgment and ability to maintain discretion and confidentiality. Ability to work independently. Ability to work and communicate effectively with a diverse population. Excellent attention to detail, problem solving, analytical, communication (verbal and written), interpersonal, and customer service skills. Understanding of organizational processes and strong follow-up skills. Must demonstrate good time management and project management skills. Work Environment Operates in an office environment, that may have frequent interruptions. The area is well-lit, temperature controlled and free from hazards.  Noise level is generally quiet to moderate. Work is primarily performed on the court/field or track, classroom or office setting. Office area is well-lit, temperature controlled and free from hazards. Travel, and work at various hours of the day or night, including early morning, overnight and weekend work is required. Physical Requirements Communicates frequently, in person, over the phone, or via a computer. Hearing is needed for extensive telephone and in person communication. Regularly required to sit for long periods of time; use hands to finger, handle or feel; reach with hands and arms. Manual dexterity is needed in order to operate a computer keyboard. Operates standard office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, filing cabinets and fax machines. Certification/Licensure CPR, 1st Aid & AED required Other important information Should teleworking become necessary, employee must be willing and able to perform all parts of this job description while working from home, on campus or a combination, and be proficient or willing to become proficient in the technology needed to work remotely. Night and weekend availability is required. Ability to drive a 15-passenger van is required. Travel to events and evaluate potential student-athlete talent, correspond with all prospects via email, phone, face to face conversations, etc. Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter and resume. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/prek-kindergarten-substitute-teacher": {
      "title": "PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher",
      "description": "PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. Position Summary Alpha House PreK & Kindergarten program at Holy Family University is seeking dedicated, dependable, and nurturing PreK and Kindergarten Substitute Teachers to support our early childhood classroom on an as-needed basis. Rooted in Catholic faith and values, our early childhood program provides a safe, structured, and faith-filled environment where young children can grow intellectually, socially, emotionally, and spiritually. The Substitute Teacher will step into implement lesson plans provided by the lead teacher, maintain classroom routine and discipline, and foster a positive, supportive learning environment aligned with Catholic teachings. Key Responsibilities & Essential Duties Faith Integration & Catholic Values Support and model Catholic values and principles throughout the school day. Lead or assist students with morning prayers, mealtime prayers, and end-of-day reflections. Encourage Christian virtues such as kindness, sharing, respect, patience, and cooperation among students. Student Care & Safety Actively supervise students at all times, including in the classroom, on the playground during recess, in hallways, and during dismissal. Attend to the social and physical needs of early childhood students with care and patience. Follow all school health, safety, and emergency protocol procedures. Communication & Record Keeping Leave detailed, professional notes for the lead teacher regarding completed lessons, student behavior, attendance, and any issues that arose during the day. Communicate politely and professionally with parents, colleagues, and school administrators as needed. Non-Essential Duties/Responsibilities Any other duties as assigned. Education & Experience Requirements High school diploma or GED required; Associate or Bachelor’s degree in Early Childhood Education, Elementary Education, or a related field preferred. Prior experience working with young children (ages 3–6) in a school, childcare, or church environment preferred. Understanding of early childhood behavior and age-appropriate learning styles. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Work Environment Operates in an office environment that may have frequent interruptions. The area is well-lit, temperature controlled and free from hazards. Noise level is generally quiet to moderate. Physical Requirements Communicates frequently, in person, over the phone, or via a computer. Hearing is needed for extensive telephone and in person communication. Regularly required to sit for long periods of time; use hands to finger, handle or feel; reach with hands and arms. Manual dexterity is needed in order to operate a computer keyboard. Ability to actively engage with young children, including bending, kneeling, sitting on the floor, and standing for extended periods. Ability to supervise indoor and outdoor play activities in various weather conditions. Operates standard office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, filing cabinets and fax machines. Certification/Licensure Strict Clearance Requirement All required local, state, federal background checks and Diocesan background clearances (including Child Abuse History Clearances, FBI Fingerprinting, and State Police Criminal Record Checks) must be fully completed and in place prior to the start of work. Completion of Diocesan Safe Environment Training / Safe Environment Certification prior to employment. CPR and First Aid Certification preferred. Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter and resume. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/registrars-office-support": {
      "title": "Registrar’s Office Support",
      "description": "Registrar’s Office Support | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Registrar’s Office Support About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Registrar’s Office Support More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth, founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown, PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County, surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. University Benefits Holy Family University takes pride in offering a range of meaningful and flexible benefits designed to promote the health and wellness of our employees and their dependents. Our comprehensive benefits and resources focus on physical, mental and financial wellness to include medical, prescription, dental and vision. We did not stop there; we also offer our employees the following fringe benefits and more. Commuter Benefits: Transit and park benefits through pre-tax payroll deductions Half-Day Fridays: Enjoy half day Fridays in the summer 403(b) Retirement: Discretionary match up to 5%; vested immediately Time Off: 12 Paid Holidays, Vacation, Personal, Sick Days and a week off for Winter Break Tuition Benefits: Employees or dependents pursuing a first Undergraduate Degree receive 100% tuition remission; employees pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 100% tuition remission; eligible dependents pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 50% tuition discount. Alpha House: 50% Discount for Nursery, Pre-K and Kindergarten Position Summary In support of the Registrar and Associate Registrars, this position is responsible for registration and administrative tasks. This position requires: technical efficiency in data entry and Microsoft Office computer skills, a student-service attitude, the ability to handle multiple tasks and ability to work cooperatively and collaboratively with university administration, faculty, staff and students. Employees must understand the mission of Catholic Higher education and be committed to the core values, mission, goals, and objectives of Holy Family University. This is an in-person position. Essential Functions Job duties that must be performed, with or without reasonable accommodation, and may include any of the following tasks, knowledge, skills and other characteristics. This position description is illustrative and is not a comprehensive listing of all functions and tasks performed by incumbents in this position. Respond to telephone calls and walk-in inquiries from students, the external community, faculty, staff and administrators on matters regarding university policies and procedures relating to records, registration, scheduling and other business conducted by the Registrar’s Office. Manage Registrar’s Office email. Processing a variety of forms and requests submitted to the Registrar’s office, including but not limited to:  Add/Drop forms, Grade Report requests, Leaves and Withdraw, Registration Populations, and Independent Study requests. Process the ad-hoc academic room requests using scheduling software (Ad Astra). As a member of the Registrar’s Office team, assist the Registrar and Assistant Registrar’s through projects focused on data integrity and usability. Maintains office supplies list and submits order requests to Registrar. Other duties as assigned. General Expectations Employees are expected to accomplish assigned duties in an efficient, effective and competent manner and to strive for improvement and excellence in all work performed.  Employees must understand the mission and demonstrate the core values of the University. Additionally, demonstrate the ability to work with diverse personalities, and harmoniously with students, faculty and staff, and the public. Employees are expected to follow and abide by all University policies, rules, regulations and guidelines. Education & Experience Requirements This position requires a high school diploma or equivalent, a bachelor’s degree is preferred. General office experience required with experience in Higher Education preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Good interpersonal communication skills are needed as this position interacts with large numbers of the external and college communities. Strong organizational skills with attention to details are required to provide efficient and effective student and data centered services. Experience with a Windows environment with an emphasis in the Microsoft Office suite including Word is required.  Experience with Excel is helpful. Good data entry skills with a high degree of accuracy are required.  A team player attitude with a willingness to learn is required. Work Environment Operates in an office environment that may have frequent interruptions. The area is well-lit, temperature controlled and free from hazards.  Noise level is generally quiet to moderate. Physical Requirements Communicates frequently, in person, over the phone, or via a computer.  Hearing is needed for extensive telephone and in person communication. Regularly required to sit for long periods of time; use hands to finger, handle or feel; reach with hands and arms. Manual dexterity is needed in order to operate a computer keyboard. Operates standard office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, filing cabinets and fax machines. Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter and resume. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/vice-dean-school-business-technology": {
      "title": "Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology",
      "description": "Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. University Benefits Holy Family University takes pride in offering a range of meaningful and flexible benefits designed to promote the health and wellness of our employees and their dependents. Our comprehensive benefits and resources focus on physical, mental and financial wellness to include medical, prescription, dental and vision. We did not stop there; we also offer our employees the following fringe benefits and more. Commuter Benefits: Transit and park benefits through pre-tax payroll deductions Half-Day Fridays: Enjoy half day Fridays in the summer 403(b) Retirement: Discretionary match up to 5%; vested immediately Time Off: 12 Paid Holidays, Vacation, Personal, Sick Days and a week off for Winter Break Tuition Benefits: Employees or dependents pursuing a first Undergraduate Degree receive 100% tuition remission; employees pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 100% tuition remission; eligible dependents pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 50% tuition discount. Alpha House: 50% Discount for Nursery, Pre-K and Kindergarten Position Summary The Vice Dean is the senior operations leader of the School of Business & Technology and a strategic partner to the Dean. The Vice Dean is responsible for managing day-to-day academic activities, leading strategic initiatives, and is the liaison for ACBSP accreditation. This critical role plays a pivotal part in enhancing the School's reputation, expanding its reach, and ensuring its programs meet the evolving needs of the business landscape. General Expectations of Holy Family University employees Uphold the mission and core values of Holy Family University, supporting the education of students to assume lifelong responsibilities towards God, society, and self. Accomplish assigned duties in an efficient, effective, and competent manner. Strive for improvement and excellence in all work performed. Demonstrate the ability to effectively interact with and work with students, faculty, staff, and the public. Follow and abide by all University policies, rules, regulations, and guidelines. If an alternative work location should become necessary, the employee must be able to perform all parts of this job description while working away from the office, on campus or a combination, and be proficient or willing to become proficient in the technology needed to work away from the office. Essential Functions Job duties must be performed, with or without reasonable accommodation, and may include any of the following tasks, knowledge, skills, and other characteristics. This position description is illustrative and is not a comprehensive listing of all functions and tasks performed by incumbents in this position. Supports the Dean in the successful deployment of strategic initiatives, including the design, implementation, support, and continuous improvement of courses, programs, and services of the School. Provides oversight and day-to-day support for faculty within the School of Business and Technology; addresses faculty requests and student issues in a timely manner. Informs the Dean of issues as appropriate. Serves as a liaison among staff, students, faculty, and the Dean. Collaborates with faculty and graduate program director to ensure program quality and effectiveness and to promote student learning, student satisfaction, enrollment, and student retention. Develops the course schedule, assigns faculty (both full-time and adjunct), and leads the hiring process for adjunct faculty. Provides support for assessment processes and program reviews. Serves as the university champion for ACBSP accreditation. Coordinates timely course observations of full time and adjunct faculty. Assists in the preparation of University materials such as the university catalog and marketing materials. Coordinates the maintenance and distribution of School-related policies and documentation. Coordinates School curriculum review, revision, and/or development. Serves as program administrator for RIZE, dual enrollment, and other specialized programs. Performs other duties as assigned by the Dean, VPAA, or President of the University. Education & Experience Requirements Master’s degree in a related business area required, doctorate preferred. At least 3 years of administrative experience in higher education. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong understanding of business and technology education at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Strong skills in project management, collaboration, critical thinking, and problem solving. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Work Environment Operates in an office environment that may have frequent interruptions. The area is well-lit, temperature controlled and free from hazards. Noise level is generally quiet to moderate. Physical Requirements Communicates frequently, in person, over the phone, or via a computer. Hearing is needed for extensive telephone and in person communication. Regularly required to sit for long periods of time; use hands to finger, handle or feel; reach with hands and arms. Manual dexterity is needed to operate a computer keyboard. Operates standard office equipment such as computers, phones, and photocopiers. Other important information Night and weekend hours to attend recruiting and student events, including but not limited to: Open Houses/Information sessions Commencement Orientation Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter and resume. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/assistant-professor-applied-behavior-analysis": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Applied Behavior Analysis",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Applied Behavior Analysis | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Assistant Professor of Applied Behavior Analysis About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Assistant Professor of Applied Behavior Analysis More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Applied Behavior Analysis Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Family Nurse Practitioner Program Director Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach Instructor or Assistant Professor of Exercise Science PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. University Benefits Holy Family University takes pride in offering a range of meaningful and flexible benefits designed to promote the health and wellness of our employees and their dependents. Our comprehensive benefits and resources focus on physical, mental and financial wellness to include medical, prescription, dental and vision. We did not stop there; we also offer our employees the following fringe benefits and more. Commuter Benefits: Transit and park benefits through pre-tax payroll deductions 403(b) Retirement: Discretionary match up to 5%; vested immediately Time Off: Paid Holidays, Sick Days and a week off for Winter Break Tuition Benefits: Employees or dependents pursuing a first Undergraduate Degree receive 100% tuition remission; employees pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 100% tuition remission; eligible dependents pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 50% tuition discount Alpha House: 50% Discount for Nursery, Pre-K and Kindergarten Position Summary The School of Arts and Sciences invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Psychology, with a start date of August 2027. All employees must understand the mission of Catholic higher education and be committed to the core values, mission, goals, and objectives of Holy Family University. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in graduate teaching.  Although the area of specialization in Behavior Analysis is open, a background in Experiential Learning is desired.  It is expected that the successful candidate will maintain a commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. The Assistant Professor of Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA) is a full-time faculty member responsible for teaching, experiential learning coordination, student advising, curriculum development, accreditation support, and community engagement. Duties and Responsibilities (not all-inclusive) Teaching courses within the Graduate Master’s in Applied Behavior Analysis Program. There is strong interest in candidates who can teach courses such as Basic Behavior Analysis, Philosophy of Behaviorism, Experiential Learning, and chair Thesis projects. Facilitating the graduate experiential learning Assisting students in understanding fieldwork hours in accordance with BACB standards Maintaining academic excellence in the classroom Advising and mentoring students in the Graduate Master’s in Applied Behavior Analysis Program Supporting accreditation and reaccreditation through ABAI including self-studies Supporting ongoing revisions to ABA program Handbook and policies Collaborating with program director to design, implement, and evaluate curriculum, ensuring it aligns with program goals and accreditation standards Sustaining an active research and scholarship agenda Participation in school- and university-wide committees, initiatives, and other service opportunities Education & Experience Requirements Candidates must hold a Psy.D., Ph.D., Ed.D., degree in behavior analysis, psychology (or a closely related field) Candidates must be a Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) Previous teaching experience 1-3 years Experience in applied behavior analysis practice, supervision, or fieldwork coordination. Experience with curriculum development, program assessment, accreditation activities, or continuous quality improvement initiatives preferred. Professional experience in applied behavior analysis is required Demonstrated ability to build partnerships with community agencies and professional organizations. Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, a statement of research interests, a list of courses taught, and complete graduate transcripts. Three letters of recommendation must be sent from the senders to the hiring manager at careers@holyfamily.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/family-nurse-practitioner-program-director": {
      "title": "Family Nurse Practitioner Program Director",
      "description": "Family Nurse Practitioner Program Director | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Family Nurse Practitioner Program Director About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Family Nurse Practitioner Program Director More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Applied Behavior Analysis Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Family Nurse Practitioner Program Director Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach Instructor or Assistant Professor of Exercise Science PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth, founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown, PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County, surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. Position Summary The FNP Program Director is a Part time position providing administrative, academic, and clinical leadership for the Family Nurse Practitioner track within the School of Nursing. This position has the administrative oversight, ensuring the program complies with national accreditation standards (e.g., CCNE) and state board regulations. The director is responsible for curriculum design, student recruitment and advising, faculty mentoring, and establishing robust clinical partnerships. The director manages the day-to-day operations of the FNP program. Key Responsibilities Academic Leadership & Curriculum Management Curriculum Oversight: Lead the development, implementation, systematic evaluation, and revision of the FNP curriculum to ensure alignment with national competencies (NONPF, AACN Essentials). Accreditation & Compliance: Maintain program compliance with regional and national accrediting bodies and State Board of Nursing requirements. Prepare self-study reports and coordinate site visits. Teaching: Able to teach in the MSN, FNP, and or DNP tracks (hybrid, or online). Student & Faculty Administration Admissions & Recruitment: Oversee the review of applicant files, interview prospective students, and make admission recommendations. Student Advisement: Guide FNP students through their plan of study, monitor academic and clinical progress, and implement remediation plans when necessary. Faculty Mentorship: Recruit, onboard, and evaluate full-time and adjunct faculty teaching within the FNP track. Clinical Coordination & Community Partnerships Placement Oversight: Collaborate with Clinical Coordinator to secure high-quality, diverse clinical sites (primary care, pediatrics, women's health) and preceptors. Site Evaluation: Ensure regular site visits and evaluations of student clinical performance and preceptor effectiveness. Community Engagement: Maintain professional relationships with healthcare networks, clinics, and professional nursing organizations to foster future clinical opportunities. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s in nursing (BSN), Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) required; Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) or Ph.D. in Nursing required. Licensure & Certification: Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) and Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) licensure in the state of employment. National board certification as a Family Nurse Practitioner (AANP or ANCC). Experience: Minimum of 3-5 years of clinical practice as an active, certified FNP. Minimum of 2–3 years of teaching experience in an accredited graduate nursing program. Prior academic leadership or administrative experience (e.g., track lead, committee chair) is highly desirable. Key Competencies Academic Leadership & Curriculum Management Curriculum Oversight: Lead the development, implementation, systematic evaluation, and revision of the FNP curriculum to ensure alignment with national competencies (NONPF, AACN Essentials). Accreditation & Compliance: Maintain program compliance with regional and national accrediting bodies and State Board of Nursing requirements. Prepare self-study reports and coordinate site visits. Teaching: Maintain a reduced teaching load in graduate-level nursing courses (hybrid, or online). Student & Faculty Administration Admissions & Recruitment: Oversee the review of applicant files, interview prospective students, and make admission recommendations. Student Advisement: Guide FNP students through their plan of study, monitor academic and clinical progress, and implement remediation plans when necessary. Faculty Mentorship: Recruit, onboard, and evaluate full-time and adjunct faculty teaching within the FNP track. Clinical Coordination & Community Partnerships Placement Oversight: Collaborate with Clinical Coordinators to secure high-quality, diverse clinical sites (primary care, pediatrics, women's health) and preceptors. Site Evaluation: Ensure regular site visits and evaluations of student clinical performance and preceptor effectiveness. Community Engagement: Maintain professional relationships with healthcare networks, clinics, and professional nursing organizations to foster future clinical opportunities. Education & Experience Requirements Leadership & Collaboration: Ability to guide diverse faculty teams and collaborate effectively across university departments. Organization: Strong project management skills to juggle accreditation deadlines, clinical rotations, and academic calendars. Communication: Exceptional written and verbal communication skills for mentoring students, drafting policies, and representing the university externally. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of graduate nursing education and Family Nurse Practitioner curriculum requirements. Strong organizational and analytical skills. Ability to interpret and apply university policies and regulatory requirements. Excellent customer service and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Proficiency in data management, report preparation, and quality improvement processes. Work Environment Primarily office-based within a School of Nursing with flexible remote working hours. Occasional evening or weekend hours for recruitment events, orientations, or accreditation activities. May require limited travel to clinical partner sites and professional meetings. Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter and resume. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://www.holyfamily.edu/about/administrative-services/human-resources/jobs/instructor-or-assistant-professor-exercise-science": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of Exercise Science",
      "description": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of Exercise Science | Holy Family University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Academics The Holy Family Experience Office for Global Initiatives Degrees and Programs Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Schools of Study Honors Program Course Catalogs Registrar Academic Support Services Career Development Services First-Generation Programs Our Faculty Library Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Adult Admissions Transfer Students Transfer Credit Calculator International Admissions Admissions Requirements Visiting Holy Family Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Admitted Students Make Your Deposit Student Experience Center for Student Life Commuting to Campus New Student Orientation Student Engagement Office The Center for Wellness and Spirituality Living on Campus Clubs & Activities Campus Ministry Dining Services Health & Wellness Philadelphia, PA Current Students About Mission Leadership News & Media Events Alumni Corporate Partners Administrative Services Faculty & Staff Campus Projects Directory Search Site Library Athletics Canvas TigerOne Help Desk Self-Service Give Apply Instructor or Assistant Professor of Exercise Science About Administrative Services Human Resources Jobs @ Holy Family University Instructor or Assistant Professor of Exercise Science More in this section Jobs @ Holy Family University Admissions Counselor/Assistant Director Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Professor of Applied Behavior Analysis Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Family Nurse Practitioner Program Director Financial Services Specialist Head Women’s Soccer Coach Instructor or Assistant Professor of Exercise Science PreK & Kindergarten Substitute Teacher Registrar’s Office Support Vice Dean - School of Business & Technology About Holy Family University Holy Family University is a sponsored ministry of the Sisters of the Holy Family of Nazareth founded in 1954. The University is a private institution in the Catholic tradition with campus locations in Philadelphia and Newtown PA. The main campus is nestled in the heart of a historic residential neighborhood in Northeast Philadelphia that is vibrant and just minutes from the excitement of Center City. The Newtown campus is located in Bucks County surrounded by nature and a step away from parks, farmers’ markets and great dining. One of the best parts of Holy Family University is our welcoming atmosphere--and that's not by chance. Our mission centers on creating an environment that encourages all members to get to know one another, learn from one another, and experience a range of perspectives and worldviews. Our community is strong because of this. University Benefits Holy Family University takes pride in offering a range of meaningful and flexible benefits designed to promote the health and wellness of our employees and their dependents. Our comprehensive benefits and resources focus on physical, mental and financial wellness to include medical, prescription, dental and vision. We did not stop there; we also offer our employees the following fringe benefits and more. Commuter Benefits: Transit and park benefits through pre-tax payroll deductions 403(b) Retirement: Discretionary match up to 5%; vested immediately Time Off: Paid Holidays, Sick Days and a week off for Winter Break Tuition Benefits: Employees or dependents pursuing a first Undergraduate Degree receive 100% tuition remission; employees pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 100% tuition remission; eligible dependents pursuing a first Master’s or Doctoral degree, receive 50% tuition discount. Alpha House: 50% Discount for Nursery, Pre-K and Kindergarten Position Summary The School of Arts and Sciences invites applications for a full-time Instructor or Assistant Professor of Exercise Science, with a start date of August 2027. All employees must understand the mission of Catholic higher education and be committed to the core values, mission, goals, and objectives of Holy Family University. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching.  Although the area of specialization is open, applications with a background in exercise science, athletic training, or a related field are encouraged to apply.  It is expected that the successful candidate will maintain a commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Duties and Responsibilities (not all-inclusive) Teaching courses within the Undergraduate Exercise Science and Biology Programs. There is strong interest in candidates who can teach courses such as, Introduction to Exercise Science, Exercise Physiology, Physical Fitness and Assessment, Strength and Conditioning, and/or Kinesiology and Biomechanics with the opportunity to develop courses in the candidate’s specialty area. Maintaining academic excellence in the classroom Advising and mentoring students in the Undergraduate Exercise Science program Sustaining an active research and scholarship agenda Participation in school- and university-wide committees, initiatives, and other service opportunities Education & Experience Requirements Candidates must hold a Masters or Doctoral Degree in Athletic Training, Exercise Science or a closely related field. Non-Discrimination Statement Holy Family University seeks to foster a welcoming and a healthy educational and work environment based on respect, the dignity of each person and the oneness of the human family. Holy Family University is dedicated to ensuring an environment free of discrimination or harassment of any kind, and promotes equal opportunity in its employment and education. Find more details on our commitment to nondiscrimination. We invite qualified applicants to view our open positions and apply directly at our career center by submitting a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, a statement of research interests, a list of courses taught, and complete graduate transcripts. Three letters of recommendation must be sent from the senders to the hiring manager at careers@holyfamily.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. A Journey of Support Find Your Program Majors & Minors Explore Our Campus Clubs & Activities Explore Resources Academic Support Start Your Application Apply Now Holy Family University - click for the homepage Philadelphia 9801 Frankford Avenue Philadelphia, PA 19114 215-637-7700 Newtown One Campus Drive Newtown, PA 18940 215-637-7700, x 4000 Contact Us Jobs @ Holy Family University Nondiscrimination Statement HEOA Accessibility Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn ©\n\t\t\t2026\n\t\t\tHoly Family University. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy"
    }
